        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0495" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 865.012/5</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Jay to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 504</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 30, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reference to previous correspondence
                    with regard to the military service cases of Enrico Ajello and Frank Ghiloni, I
                    have the honor to transmit herewith translation of a Foreign Office note
                    received today concerning both of these cases, from which it will be seen that
                    the Minister of War reaffirms his prior decisions in cases of this nature.</p>
                <p>His decision seems to be based upon the fact that the provisions of the law of
                    June 13, 1912, No. 555 (this is the law promulgated June 30, 1912), are not
                    retroactive and can not be availed of by those who became liable to military
                    service prior to the enactment thereof.</p>
                <p>It will be noticed that the note states that Enrico Ajello has already left
                    Italy.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peter S. Jay</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d487-a1.xml" xpointer="d487-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
